];
``

Wait, one problem: OUTAGE_CODE_RE `\b(5\d{2}|429)\b` would also match inside model names? e.g. "glm-5.3-flash"? No — \b5\d{2}\b on "glm-5.3-flash": "5.3" — 5 followed by '.', not a digit. OK. What about "330s"? No. What about timestamps? Some noise possible; acceptable — codes extraction is for a comment, minor noise ok. But wait — over-matching: "after 6 attempt(s) over 330s" — no. "2026-10-19" — no 3-digit. OK.

Dedupe + order-preserved collection, cap at 6.

```js
function collectMatches(text, re, cap) {
   var found = [];
   var seen = {};
   re.lastIndex = 0;
   var m;
   while ((m = re.exec(text)) !== null) {
       var value = m[1];
       if (value && !seen[value]) {
           seen[value] = true;
           found.push(value);
           if (found.length >= cap) break;
       }
   }
   re.lastIndex = 0;
   return found;
}

function extractOutageModels(text) {
   var models = [];
   OUTAGE_MODEL_RES.forEach(function (re) {
       collectMatches(text, re, 6).forEach(function (model) {
           if (models.indexOf(model) === -1) models.push(model);
       });
   });
   return models;
}

function extractOutageCodes(text) {
   return collectMatches(text, OUTAGE_CODE_RE, 6);
}
``

Hmm — wait, the third model pattern `provider\s*[:\["']+\s*([A-Za-z0-9][\w.-]*)` — for text "Provider chain exhausted: 2 of 2..." — `provider` followed by `[:\["']+`? After "Provider" comes " chain" — a space, not in the class `[:\["']+`. No match. Good. But `provider: zai` shape matches. OK.

Edge: the second pattern with `[\w-]{2,}` — "kimi-for-coding then hit 429" → captures "kimi-for-coding". ✓. But could it capture garbage like "attempt" in "attempt then hit 429"? Unlikely text. Fine.

Now classifyFailure ordering:

```js
function classifyFailure(text) {
   var t = String(text || '');
   if (!t.trim()) return null;
   var window = extractQuotaWindow(t);
   // Quota ALWAYS wins ... (unchanged, I1)
   if (hasQuotaEvidence(t, window)) {
       return { kind: 'quota_exhausted', ... };
   }
   // gh-1121: an exhausted-chain tail whose attempts are only transient
   // (5xx / 429 / network — no 401 auth text) is a provider OUTAGE, not a
   // bare blip: the dev leg may resume the persisted session once instead
   // of cold-reseting. At this point quota/403 evidence is already
   // excluded by the priority branch above.
   if (CHAIN_EXHAUSTED_RE.test(t) && !AUTH_CODE_RE.test(t)) {
       var models = extractOutageModels(t);
       return {
           kind: 'provider_transient',
           provider: models[0] || extractProvider(t),
           models: models,
           codes: extractOutageCodes(t),
           window: null,
           evidence: 'provider chain exhausted'
       };
   }
   if (RATE_LIMIT_RE.test(t) || TIMEOUT_RE.test(t)) {
       return { kind: 'transient', ... };
   }
   return null;
}
