];
``

Wait, one problem: OUTAGE_CODE_RE `\b(5\d{2}|429)\b` would also match inside model names? e.g. "glm-5.3-flash"? No — \b5\d{2}\b on "glm-5.3-flash": "5.3" — 5 followed by '.', not a digit. OK. What about "330s"? No. What about timestamps? Some noise possible; acceptable — codes extraction is for a comment, minor noise ok. But wait — over-matching: "after 6 attempt(s) over 330s" — no. "2026-10-19" — no 3-digit. OK.

Dedupe + order-preserved collection, cap at 6.

```js
function collectMatches(text, re, cap) {
   var found = [];
   var seen = {};
   re.lastIndex = 0;
   var m;
   while ((m = re.exec(text)) !== null) {
       var value = m[1];
       if (value && !seen[value]) {
           seen[value] = true;
           found.push(value);
           if (found.length >= cap) break;
       }
   }
   re.lastIndex = 0;
   return found;
}

function extractOutageModels(text) {
   var models = [];
   OUTAGE_MODEL_RES.forEach(function (re) {
       collectMatches(text, re, 6).forEach(function (model) {
           if (models.indexOf(model) === -1) models.push(model);
       });
   });
   return models;
}

function extractOutageCodes(text) {
   return collectMatches(text, OUTAGE_CODE_RE, 6);
}
``

