3 failures:
1. "explicit missingResponse.enabled=false still opts out" — the sleep runs BEFORE the enablement check inside resumeOnceForMissingResponse. Design flaw: the backoff should only run when the resume will actually be attempted. Fix: check the opt-out BEFORE sleeping — i.e. `resumeOnceForProviderOutage` should perform the same explicit-disable check first, or resumeOnceForMissingResponse should take a pre-backoff callback... Cleanest: compute the gate first. I'll hoist the sleep to AFTER a gate check by restructuring: `resumeOnceForProviderOutage` checks `providerOutageResumeDisabled(customParams)` — a small helper miroring the scoped.enabled===false check:

```js
function providerOutageResumeOptedOut(customParams) {
   var root = (customParams && customParams.feedbackLoop) || {};
   var scoped = (root.missingResponse && typeof root.missingResponse === 'object') ? root.missingResponse : {};
   return scoped.enabled === false;
}
``

